# Fitted thickness parameters of the H = 80 mm stack, one row per section, root first
# written      : 28 Sep 2026 with the X_geom section fit (control.py settings)
# source       : Rudder/outputs/sections_stack_y0_y80_raw_mm.dat (Wind_Tunnel_Rudder.stp, 50 horizontal
#                sections from y = 0 to 80 mm, step 80/49 mm); section 1 is the root, as in sections_xcad_m.dat
# companion    : thickness_params_H80.txt (Section # | X1 | X2 | T1 | T2 | r), same numbers
# parameters   : quartic Bezier half-section P0 (0,0), P1 (0,T1), P2 (X1,T1), P3 (X2,T2), P4 (1,0), mirrored
#                for the lower surface, with its sharp TE rounded by the circle of radius r tangent to it.
#                X1, X2, T1, T2, r are fractions of the sharp chord cs_mm (P4 is the sharp TE). In the fit code
#                they are X2, X3, Y1, Y3 and the fillet radius; T1 and T2 are half-thickness ordinates.
# fit          : Main_PSO (swarm 50, 100 iterations, constriction factor, clip to bounds, seed 42) then a
#                bounded least-squares polish; bounds Y1 [0, 0.15], X2 [0.05, 0.5], X3 [0.3, 0.95], Y3 [0, 0.15];
#                fillet_method 0 (circle tangent to the replica where the original's TE fillet starts)
# note         : X2 sits on its 0.3 lower bound in every section
# columns
#   section      section number, 1 = root (y = 0)
#   y_mm         span station
#   chord_mm     section chord (LE to rounded TE)
#   cs_mm        sharp chord, the length the five parameters are fractions of
#   X1 X2 T1 T2 r  as in thickness_params_H80.txt
#   r_mm         fitted TE radius; R_orig_mm the original section's TE radius
#   fit_um       RMS vertical gap to the sharpened section at its points (the objective)
#   gap_rms_um   RMS and largest normal distance of the original's upper-surface points
#   gap_max_um   to the fitted foil (TE rounded)
#   rle_fit_mm   LE radius of the fit, 4 T1^2 / (3 X1) * cs; rle_orig_mm the original's
#
